      "text": "In this book, the prophet Isaiah delivers a challenging prophecy about the nation of Israel, much of which relates to events we will see in the end times (the Book of Revelation is full of wonders). The most significant message Isaiah conveys is the prophecy of a Savior. During this time, the Babylonians were rapidly gaining world dominance. God could have subdued this nation and maintained Israel’s supremacy (as He did with the Assyrians in Hezekiah’s time), but He chose to allow the Babylonians to rise to power and conquer Israel. Why? Isaiah explains this. I consider this to be a “fifth” gospel, if you will (first of five). Isaiah provides detailed insights into the coming of the Messiah of Israel.",
