  "isaiah_32_10": [
    {
      "id": "isaiah_32_10_isaiah-32-9-15_1587",
      "book": "Isaiah",
      "chapter": 32,
      "verse": 10,
      "startVerse": 9,
      "endVerse": 15,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "There will be trouble on this Earth. Isaiah isn’t sugarcoating it. God, ultimately, has revealed everything that will take place. He is warning the people of Israel here, but (honestly) we are the ones that must heed the warnings. It is all broughten back up again in Revelation. God doesn’t make us go through anything without warning.",
      "likes": 0,
      "isLikedByUser": false,
      "isBookmarkedByUser": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z",
      "kind": "comment",
      "quoteStyle": null,
      "sectionId": "isaiah-32-9-15",
      "sectionTitle": "Freedom Rings",
      "isIntroduction": false,
      "verseLabel": "10-12"
    },
    {
      "id": "isaiah_32_10_isaiah-32-9-15_1588",
      "book": "Isaiah",
      "chapter": 32,
      "verse": 10,
      "startVerse": 9,
      "endVerse": 15,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "How many years and decades would it take for the whole world to finally accept the warnings and turn towards the Lord? Apparently, it will never happen. We don’t like to listen. We are rebellious towards God. By the fact that Isaiah has to tell them to be troubled and to “gird sackcloth” proves that no one actually cares about what God is telling them. They are living fancy and fine lives without the Lord.",
      "likes": 0,
      "isLikedByUser": false,
      "isBookmarkedByUser": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z",
      "kind": "comment",
      "quoteStyle": null,
      "sectionId": "isaiah-32-9-15",
      "sectionTitle": "Freedom Rings",
      "isIntroduction": false,
      "verseLabel": "10-12"
    },
    {
      "id": "isaiah_32_10_isaiah-32-9-15_1589",
      "book": "Isaiah",
      "chapter": 32,
      "verse": 10,
      "startVerse": 9,
      "endVerse": 15,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "But when the Lord starts taking things away from them, they are all going to wish they had paid closer attention when they had the chance. Same goes for us.",
      "likes": 0,
      "isLikedByUser": false,
      "isBookmarkedByUser": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z",
      "kind": "comment",
      "quoteStyle": null,
      "sectionId": "isaiah-32-9-15",
      "sectionTitle": "Freedom Rings",
      "isIntroduction": false,
      "verseLabel": "10-12"
    }
  ],
  "isaiah_32_13": [
    {
      "id": "isaiah_32_13_isaiah-32-9-15_1590",
      "book": "Isaiah",
      "chapter": 32,
      "verse": 13,
      "startVerse": 9,
      "endVerse": 15,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "Things will look very bleak and sad in their future. Things will look bleak and sad for us as well. Actually, today, things are quite bleak and sad in our world. I don’t think there is any nation that is living in “prosperity” today. The US is eroding every second of every day. It would be a miracle to see the cost of living get easier in our country, but I don’t think I’m going to see that in my lifetime. Perhaps the Lord is preparing His coming again? I don’t know. But we will see (and already should know at this point) that God is going to have His way with Israel.",
      "likes": 0,
      "isLikedByUser": false,
      "isBookmarkedByUser": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z",
      "kind": "comment",
      "quoteStyle": null,
      "sectionId": "isaiah-32-9-15",
      "sectionTitle": "Freedom Rings",
      "isIntroduction": false,
      "verseLabel": "13-14"
    },
    {
      "id": "isaiah_32_13_isaiah-32-9-15_1591",
      "book": "Isaiah",
      "chapter": 32,
      "verse": 13,
      "startVerse": 9,
      "endVerse": 15,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "All these things have come to pass. The palaces are forsaken, the cities were left in multitudes, the forts and towers became nothing more than shelters for wild animals. They lost everything. They will come back to the land, but they will still be owned by Rome when they do. There is only one thing that can help them, can you guess what it is? It’s listed in our next verse:",
      "likes": 0,
      "isLikedByUser": false,
      "isBookmarkedByUser": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z",
      "kind": "comment",
      "quoteStyle": null,
      "sectionId": "isaiah-32-9-15",
      "sectionTitle": "Freedom Rings",
      "isIntroduction": false,
      "verseLabel": "13-14"
    }
  ],
